{"schema_version":1,"title":"Per-dispatch stage timeout with orch-sequential retirement","goal":"Kill every hung run hook at its per-stage limit on every dispatch route, end it timed_out, and retire the orch-sequential backend that silently discards the limit it is given","steps":[{"id":"step-1","description":"Strengthen the five partial-SPEC assertions so each asserts what is required, not what the code happens to do: verify the always_run and parallel-group dispatch routes reach the watchdog (SPEC-1); add an isolation run that sets neither template value nor ZBUILD_STAGE_TIMEOUT_S and confirms 5400 s is actually used (SPEC-3); add a live dispatch that runs longer than 300 s inside its stage_timeout_s and completes (SPEC-7); assert the unreadable-config path produces output naming the backend, not only a non-zero exit (SPEC-9); assert event-schema-emitted-coverage-test passes after registration (SPEC-18).","areas":["tests/unit/stage-timeout-dispatch-test.sh","tests/unit/stage-timeout-precedence-test.sh","tests/unit/orch-backend-misconfigured-test.sh","tests/unit/stage-timeout-no-flat-limit-test.sh"]},{"id":"step-2","description":"Amend ADR-054 §9, ADR-017, and ADR-011 with the new statements (stage_timeout_s surface, one-model-call meaning of router.timeout_s, orch-sequential retirement, misconfigured-on-missing-backend) and add an ## Enforced by entry naming the test for each new statement; remove those three ADRs from config/adr-enforcement-baseline.txt (the file only shrinks).","areas":["docs/adr/ADR-054-stage-contract.md","docs/adr/ADR-017-per-stage-router-config.md","docs/adr/ADR-011-pluggable-backends.md","config/adr-enforcement-baseline.txt"]},{"id":"step-3","description":"Parse and validate stage_timeout_s in the template loader alongside router.timeout_s — apply the three-tier fallback (template field > ZBUILD_STAGE_TIMEOUT_S > 5400 s), reject a value that is not a positive integer or is below the same stage's router.timeout_s, and expose it through the existing getter pattern.","areas":["core/pipeline/template.sh"]},{"id":"step-4","description":"Fix the per-dispatch timer in lifecycle.sh: scope process-group mode to the plugin subshell only so the calling runner shell job-control flag is unchanged (fixes the monitor-mode-ON test failure); remove the remaining hand-rolled kill -KILL line after wait and route all stage killing through zbuild_pg_kill (fixes SPEC-10); the watchdog arms on the run hook only, cancels on normal exit, and writes a timed_out disposition naming the stage and the limit on expiry.","areas":["core/plugin-registry/lifecycle.sh","scripts/lib/proc-group.sh"]},{"id":"step-5","description":"Fix the always_run watchdog in runner.sh: replace the hand-rolled TERM/KILL sequence with zbuild_pg_kill so a hook child that ignores TERM is killed within the grace window (fixes SPEC-6b); read the per-stage timeout from stage_timeout_s rather than router.timeout_s for the dispatch limit (Decision 4).","areas":["core/pipeline/runner.sh"]},{"id":"step-6","description":"Migrate the local-engine kill path to zbuild_pg_kill — replace the per-PID single-signal helper in local_engine.sh with the shared process-group helper for consistent TERM-then-KILL behaviour at 10 s grace.","areas":["core/orch/local_engine.sh"]},{"id":"step-7","description":"Remove the flat ZBUILD_ORCH_TIMEOUT collect deadline from all three strategy files so no backend collect timeout undercuts a stage's stage_timeout_s; the per-dispatch timer in lifecycle.sh becomes the only stage-level bound.","areas":["core/pipeline/strategies/fanout.sh","core/pipeline/strategies/map.sh","core/pipeline/strategies/sequential.sh"]},{"id":"step-8","description":"Retire orch-sequential: delete the plugin directory, its golden file, and its wiki page; harden the backend loader in contract.sh to treat a missing backend or an unreadable config as a hard misconfigured error (no silent fallback); migrate the unit tests that used orch-sequential as a fixture to orch-mock so the suite stays green.","areas":["plugins/tool/orch-sequential/","core/orch/contract.sh","docs/wiki/Plugins.md","docs/wiki/plugins/orch-sequential.md","tests/golden/orch-sequential-capabilities.golden","tests/unit/summary-mandatory-test.sh","tests/unit/dispatch-rc-guard-test.sh","tests/unit/stdin-spawn-guard-test.sh","tests/unit/core-orch-run-id-isolation-test.sh","tests/unit/adr059-no-tmpdir-defaults-test.sh","tests/unit/plugin-artifact-goldens-test.sh"]},{"id":"step-9","description":"Add the measured stage_timeout_s values to simple.yaml for every named stage per the issue table; move the always_run release and persist stages from router.timeout_s to stage_timeout_s at their current values (30 s / 120 s) so Decision 4 is live in the running template.","areas":["config/templates/simple.yaml"]},{"id":"step-10","description":"Update the 10 test files that shape-floor identified as still spelling out counts, orders, or lists altered by this change — the two golden event-sequence files and the eight unit test files that pin template field counts or stage lists — so that npm test passes on the new simple.yaml shape.","areas":["tests/golden/full-pipeline/event-sequence.golden","tests/golden/parity/event-sequence.golden","tests/unit/shape-floor-content-stable-test.sh","tests/unit/template-simple-yaml-test.sh","tests/unit/build-oos-pass-request-test.sh","tests/unit/change-scope-floor-test.sh","tests/unit/core-pipeline-template-test.sh","tests/unit/template-resolvability-preflight-test.sh","tests/unit/impact-prefilter-order-detector-test.sh","tests/unit/shape-floor-summary-plain-test.sh"]}],"open_questions":["SPEC-7 live-completion test: which mechanism besides the retired ZBUILD_ORCH_TIMEOUT collect deadline could still fire within 300 s and kill the dispatch before stage_timeout_s expires?","SPEC-1 parallel-group route: does the parallel-group member dispatch path call plugin_hook_call directly through template.sh or via runner.sh, and is that route covered by the existing assertion?"]}
